stablished and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 44 Consulting Pathologist s   Grace T  McKee MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axilla and breast  is a 40 x 26 x 5cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 25 x 18cm overlying skin ellipse and 14 x 11 x 3cm axillary content  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a poorly defined 8 x 5 x 4cm area at the medial aspect of the specimen  which appears to be firm with multiple punctate areas of hard consistency  No biopsy site is identified  The remaining breast tissue is fibrofatty  Multiple axillary lymph nodes  ranging from 0 3cm x 1 2cm in largest dimension  are identified  Representative sections are submitted  Section code  A F  Sampling of the firm area G  Deep resection margin en face  representative sections H I  Representative sections from unremarkable breast tissue J  One bisected lymph node K  Trisected lymph node L  One bisected lymph node M  Lymph nodes N Q  One bisected lymph node in each R  Lymph nodes S X  Additional sections of the firm area  Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Sarah P Thayer  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  5 CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows as dispersed  small nests throughout a mass spanning five centimeters  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF TEN LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus consists of a few cells in the subcapsular sinus  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm in greatest dimension  A skin ellipse with central nipple is attached with a long stitch at one end of the skin ellipse  and a short stitch ninety degrees away  The long stitch is parallel to an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fibroadipose appendage to the bulk of the specimen  Two small fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  6 0cm in greatest dimension are received  A central area of hard  irregularly outlined  white tan tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm in greatest dimension  0 9cm from the closest  deep  resection margin  The rest of the parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections of the hard mass are in A E  Representative sections of adjacent areas of breast parenchyma are in F J  Ten lymph nodes from the  appendage  of the specimen parallel to the long stitch range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  A section of each node is in K M  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Positive.
