est s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 07 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab and identified by the surgeon is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm irregular portion of breast with a long suture on the lateral end and short stitch on the superior aspect  The entire specimen is inked blue with its deep margin overinked yellow  Sectioning reveals a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity surrounded by a 0 3cm rim of firm white tissue  which comes to 0 5cm from the posterior medial margin  Focal granularity is present in the remaining parenchyma  SECTION CODE A D  Entire biopsy cavity from inferior to superior with closest posterior margin  E F  Superior breast parenchyma representative section  Labeled  left axillary sentinel node  are two REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm pair of yellow tan soft tissue nodules  Each nodule is bisected and submitted in G and H  Labeled  left axillary non sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yellow tan round soft tissue nodule  bisected and entirely submitted in I  Labeled  left breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow tan irregular soft tissue fragment  Entirely submitted in J through M  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY CAVITY WITH SURROUNDING FIRM TISSUE  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM POSTERIOMEDIAL MARGIN                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY NON SENTINEL  EXCISION PART C  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOP , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 34 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SIX OF SIX LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 46                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The attached skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  The nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and is centrally retracted  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Sectioning reveals a white firm lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm which grossly approaches the closest resection margin which is the deep resection margin to 1 2cm  Section Code  A B  lesion with closest margin  C D E  representative sections through the lesion  F  nipple  G  lesion with superior resection margin  H  nipple  A separate stellate  white  firm lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and 1 0cm from the deep margin  is present  Representative sections from this lesion are in L O  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Ten node like structures are identified in the axillary tail and representative sections from each are submitted in cassettes I  J  and K  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Barbara J Kane  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Positive.
