Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 45 CLINICAL DATA  Microcalcifications  abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  EXTENSIVE INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2 8CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIPLE FOCI  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU COMEDO TYPE WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  MULTIPLE FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No infiltrating ductal carcinoma is identified  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 23 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with an attached localizing wire and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm white nodule  grossly extending to multiple inked margins  A representative section of the nodule is frozen and saved frozen  The remainder of the nodular area is submitted entirely in cassettes A F  Representative sections of the remaining grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma submitted in cassettes G J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David Bent Smith  M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
