Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 24 CLINICAL DATA  61 year old with right breast nodule and saline implants                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIAMETER MEASURED FROM SLIDE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE TUMOR AND TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 25                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of breast  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a white pink  ill defined firm nodule occupying the whole specimen  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette A  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
