er quadrant  which extends to 0 7cm from the anterior margin and 3 3cm from the posterior margin and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm poorly delineated nodular fibrous area in the central lower to mid breast  which extends to 2 0cm from the posterior margin and is 3 5cm from the first described nodule  The lower outer quadrant contains several gritty firm tan foci as large as REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  which extend to 0 3cm from the posterior margin  The lateral tissue contains one small lymph node  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multinodular fibrous area in central lower to mid breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant including firm tan foci   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections  Unfixed  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  left breast   is an 18 x 16 x 4 0cm left mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a 15 x 5 6cm ellipse of skin with an unremarkable areola and nipple  A suture designates the superolateral aspect  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen contains four nodules  The first occupies the  11 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  and extends to 0 2cm from the posterior margin and 0 4cm from the anterior margin  It consists of indurated  triangular  gray white and centrally hemorrhagic tissue  The second sits 4 0cm inferomedial to the first  occupies the  8 o clock  position  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x o 7cm  and extends to 0 4cm from the posterior margin  The mass appears well defined  feels indurated  and consists of tan white and focally hemorrhagic tissue  The third mass occupies the  7 o clock  position at a distance of 0 9cm from the second mass and 6 3cm from the third mass  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and extends to 0 7cm of the posterior margin and 1 5cm of the anterior margin  The final mass occupies the  9 o clock  position  sits 0 7cm superior to the second mass and 3 0cm from the first mass  spans REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and extends to 0 7cm from the posterior margin  It consists of soft  well circumscribed  tan pink tissue  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   11 o clock mass  mass  1  from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue between masses  1 and  2 and between masses  2 and  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   8 o clock mass  mass  2    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue between mass  2  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass at 7 o clock  mass  3   Unfixed  in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  sentinel lymph node   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of yellow tan soft tissue containing 1 lymph node  which is entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional left axillary sentinel node  247   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fat containing 3 lymph nodes from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  which are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional axillary sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm slightly firm  lymph node  which is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In fixative  labeled  Leslie S  Stein  REMOVED_DATE  additional left axillary sentinel node  270   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node  which is entirely submitted in cas