UCTAL HYPERPLASIA 2  RADIAL SCAR 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA 4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  gross and microscopic measurement   GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Positive along a broad front at the superior margin of the specimen  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NOTE  Sections of the right breast excision  part B  reveal invasive carcinoma growing in broad trabeculae and small nests of tumor cells with large geographic zones of keratinaceous necrosis and desmoplasia  The tumor cells are large with abundant dense keratinizing cytoplasm and have large central hyperchromatic nuclei with marked contour irregularities  vesicular chromatin and prominent macronucleoli  There is no tubule formation  Numerous mitotic figures  including atypical mitoses  are present  The morphologic findings are those of a high grade invasive ductal carcinoma with prominent squamous differentiation  also known as a metaplastic carcinoma  The extensive keratinization and cytomorphology are compatible with the large cell keratinizing variant of metaplastic carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm soft tissue fragment  The adipose tissue is dissected to reveal 3 lymph nodes  Lymph node  1 is 1cm in greatest dimension and is not inked  Lymph node  2 is 0 9cm in greatest dimension and is inked blue  Lymph node  3 is 0 8cm in greatest dimension and is inked black  All 3 lymph nodes are bisected and submitted entirely as FX  1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm piece of fibroa