 progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 39     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THE LYMPH NODES DO NOT CONTAIN KERATIN POSITIVE CARCINOMA CELLS  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary nodes  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm skin ellipse attached  On the surface of the skin is an inverted nipple  with apparently no areolar complex  Superior and lateral to the nipple is a hard white  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nodule that comes to within 3 0cm of the skin  Sections of the nodule are submitted in cassettes A  B  and C  Away from the nodule is an area with a mottled white pink and yellow surface  It is not firm  Sections submitted in cassette D  The rest of the breast tissue is unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes E and F  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes G through K  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Positive.
