tomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of tan yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 9 5cm tan white skin ellipse with a paracentral 3 5cm circular inverted nipple  There is a 2 0cm well healed scar 3 0cm from the nipple  There are 3 tan yellow nodular skin lesions ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm that approach the margin of skin  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular tan  firm tumor 1 0cm from the deep margin  There is a 0 4cm linear defect within the tumor consistent with a previous biopsy site  The remaining cut surface consists of approximately 70  glistening yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30  dense gray white fibrous tissue  Lymph nodes within the upper outer quadrant are not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor  E  Section of breast away from tumor  F  Skin lesions  Gross Description by  MARTY STONE Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  01 AUG 94 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  Suspicious mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  25    MULTIPLE FOCI  ARISING OUT OF EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  75    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Most of the 7cm  biopsy specimen consists of in situ ductal carcinoma  Three foci of invasive carcinoma are present  which are REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  and 0 1cm in greatest dimension  respectively  Invasive and in situ carcinoma extend to the resection margin  including the margin designated  subareolar margin   There is no evidence of lymphatic invasion  Hormone receptor studies will be performed by immunoperoxidase and will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  08 AUG 94 at 12 05                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 94 at 07 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and suture designating the subareola margin  The specimen is inked green at the subareola margin and black elsewhere  The specimen is bisected longitudinally to reveal a pink tan  firm  lobulated mass with scant focal hemorrhage and irregular borders extending diffusely to the inked margins  Representative section frozen as FX 1  and submitted in A  Representative sections of the tumor expanding from the subareola margin to the opposite margin are submitted in B through J  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST LEFT MASS   LOBULAR CARCINOMA OF BREAST  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS , Positive.
