Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Levels Examined Reason for Addendum  4  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Invasive left breast carcinoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  calponin  smooth muscle myosin heavy chain  and cytokeratin confirm that areas of papillary carcinoma represent papillary ductal carcinoma in situ rather than invasive tumor  A few rounded areas of carcinoma lack identifiable myoepithelial cells on immunostains  the possibility that these represent additional microscopic foci of invasive carcinoma with blunt invasion cannot be excluded  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Two main nodules  1 0cm and 0 5cm  with a few satellite foci measuring  0 1cm to 0 25cm  A few additional foci of blunt invasion between 0 1cm and 0 2cm in size cannot be entirely excluded  see note above   GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  a few foci  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to the anterior margin and is 0 15cm from the superior margin  Invasive tumor may also extend to  0 1cm from the lateral margin  additional studies to evaluate this margin will be reported in an addendum  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1 to 2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Full panel requested on the 0 5cm nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    repeat Her 2 requested on the previously biopsied 1 0cm nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    See also  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  1  MULTIPLE SMALL FOCI OF INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT THE INKED NEW MARGIN  2  FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING TO THE INKED NEW MARGIN  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   NOTE  The foci of invasive carcinoma in this specimen resemble the larger tumor in the main excision  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast lumpectomy  short   superior  long   lateral   is an REMOVED_DATE  A P  x REMOVED_DATE  M L  x REMOVED_DATE  S I cm breast excision specimen oriented with a short stitch superior and a long stitch left lateral  2 needle localization wires are present in the specimen  both of which pass into the medial aspect  one anteriorly and one posteriorly  The wires are removed and the specimen is inked per protocol as follows  Superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the anterior posterior axis into 11 slices numbered from posterior to anterior  An ill defined tan pink area of fibrosis  cystic change  and nodularity is present in slice  6  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and approaches to 0 7cm from the inferior margin  1 5cm from the superior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  2 0cm from the medial margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and 3 4cm from the anterior margin  A biopsy tract is passing through this area and a clip is identified in slice  5 adjacent to the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Slice  1  representa