Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 45 CLINICAL DATA  79 year old female with history of infiltrating lobular carcinoma of the left breast  and now with a right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SEGMENTAL EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95   REMOVED_DATE CM BY GROSS EXAM  REMOVED_DATE CM MEASURED FROM SLIDES  GRADE 2  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5   SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INFILTRATING TUMOR TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURFACE OF THE LARGER FRAGMENT  AND SEVERAL SEPARATE FOCI WITHIN THE SMALLER FRAGMENT  TWO OF WHICH ARE AT INKED SURFACES  3  DUCTAL TYPE EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND A SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMA  4  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC VASCULAR SCLEROSIS  NOTE  The invasive tumor  present in the larger fragment  is well delineated  and while close to an inked surface  does not appear to have been incised  In the other fragment  carcinoma in situ spans a region 2 0cm in diameter measured from slide E  and is present at inked surfaces  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor stains will be performed  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   are two fragments of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The larger fragment contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan white  granular  ill defined firm mass  0 25cm from the inked resection margin  The remainder of both fragments are unremarkable  A section of tumor is frozen as FX 1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Additional sections of the tumor are submitted in B D  Two sections of the small fragment are submitted in cassettes E and F  A small portion of specimen was taken for research at Dr  Sgroi s lab  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  SUGGESTIVE OF DUCTAL  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS TO RULE OUT LOBULAR  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
