Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 52 CLINICAL DATA  Prior left breast cancer  now with a right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  LOW GRADE  FEW SMALL NESTS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND EXTENDING TO MARGIN OF SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The sclerosis surrounding the in situ carcinoma distorts the glandular architecture and makes the evaluation of invasion difficult  Nevertheless  a few small nests of malignant cells seem to infiltrate into the stroma  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins appear free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm soft pink tan piece of tissue  It is inked and breadloafed to reveal rubbery white tissue with focal grittiness  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes A through D  Cassette A contains a possible calcification  Cassette B contains a possible fibrous lesion  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR IS IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
