 with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 40     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Multiple immunohistochemical stains for keratin show no keratin positive tumor cells in the lymph nodes  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  24 AUG 98 at 14 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  mass  left axilla plus left axillary sampling   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue showing a central poorly circumscribed  white  hard branching area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen surfaces are inked and representative sections are submitted in Cassettes A C  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of adipose tissue  containing two lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 5cm  Grossly  the lymph nodes are soft with fatty changes  The larger lymph node is submitted in Cassette D  the smaller in Cassette E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision  left breast   and with a note  old cavity went to pectoralis muscle   is a REMOVED_DATE x REM